<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kabul</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kabul is a city in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, strategically placed on routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>, the last Timurid prince expelled from Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, took Kabul and used it as his base. From there he invaded India and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, as Timurid rule in Central Asia came to an end.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kabul.jpg" alt="Kabul" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Weaveravel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kabul,_Afghanistan_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
